# Build output and local dev artifacts -- rebuilt inside the image itself.
node_modules
dist

# Real data never belongs in the image. `data/` is where the dev SQLite
# file lives; `*.db*` catches one anywhere else on disk; `.superpowers/`
# is this project's own planning/task-tracking tree (specs, task briefs,
# session notes -- some of which discuss real holdings by name); and
# `fixtures/real/` is a path convention reserved for real (as opposed to
# synthetic/anonymised) broker exports, should one ever be added under
# that name, even though none exists in the repo today. The user's actual
# broker exports were deliberately deleted from this repo entirely --
# this list is defense in depth, not the only thing standing between a
# real export and a built image.
data
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.superpowers
**/fixtures/real/**

# Secrets. `.env.example` is a template with no real secret in it and is
# NOT excluded; `.env`/`.env.local` (git-ignored, holds the real
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET) must never be copied into a build layer, even
# though only the runtime stage's explicit COPY list -- not this file --
# decides what reaches the final image; this stops it reaching the build
# stage's layers at all.
.env
.env.local

.git

# Not needed to build or run the image.
docs
e2e
tools
